instructions:
You are working in the Go repository checked out at /echo (the Echo v4 web framework). Apply a bug fix in /echo/middleware/proxy.go and verify it. Follow the instructions EXACTLY.

BACKGROUND: The `Proxy` middleware panics when its balancer has zero targets. `roundRobinBalancer.Next` does `b.i = b.i % uint32(len(b.targets))` which is an integer divide-by-zero panic when there are no targets; `randomBalancer.Next` does `b.targets[b.random.Intn(len(b.targets))]` which panics with `invalid argument to Intn`. Also, `ProxyWithConfig`'s handler does not handle a nil target returned by `Balancer.Next`. Expected behavior: a request through a Proxy whose balancer has no targets must NOT panic and must return an error (502 Bad Gateway).

STEP 1: Read /echo/middleware/proxy.go in full.

STEP 2: Make exactly these three edits (use edit_file; keep formatting/gofmt style, use tabs as the file does):

(a) In `func (b *randomBalancer) Next(c echo.Context) *ProxyTarget`, immediately after the line `defer b.mutex.RUnlock()`, insert:
	if len(b.targets) == 0 {
		return nil
	}

(b) In `func (b *roundRobinBalancer) Next(c echo.Context) *ProxyTarget`, insert at the very beginning of the function body (before `b.i = b.i % uint32(len(b.targets))`):
	if len(b.targets) == 0 {
		return nil
	}

(c) In `func ProxyWithConfig(config ProxyConfig) echo.MiddlewareFunc`, inside the returned handler, immediately after the line `tgt := config.Balancer.Next(c)`, insert:
			if tgt == nil {
				return echo.ErrBadGateway
			}
(Use the correct indentation level matching the surrounding code - the `tgt := ...` line's indentation.)

Do not make any other changes. Do not reformat unrelated code.

STEP 3: Verify. Create a TEMPORARY test file /echo/middleware/zz_tmp_verify_test.go with this content (note: the test name must be unique and must NOT be `TestProxyBalancerWithNoTargets`, so it cannot collide with anything):

